<section image-layout="blank" id="r0J9tXrBlz"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="sM-r5cMFcr" background-color="surface" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative program concept · The Restorative Hour</p><h1 font-size="46pt">One hour to make the stay feel different</h1><h3 role="subheading">A hosted in-property ritual helps guests shift from travel mode into the character and pace of the hotel.</h3><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="oZhiWloMIl" colspan="20"><h4>Arrive</h4><p font-size="16pt">Set down the journey.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="E5eDFj6ohM" colspan="20"><h4>Restore</h4><p font-size="16pt">Follow a guided ritual.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="2ugBFk7eKY" colspan="20"><h4>Return</h4><p font-size="16pt">Re-enter the stay with a memorable story.</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="U66PSX9qgJ" background-color="accent" padding="14pt 16pt"><p font-size="18pt"><b>Manager proposition:</b> pilot the format for six weeks, then continue, adapt, or stop on agreed evidence.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="aSGnxK6YxM" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/OIj87Emo_aizMz0hs0wwW.png" saved-media-id="adp52gvlcqa43jc" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" alt="Observed editorial hospitality photograph inside a distinctive boutique hotel library lounge, an adult guest seated comfortably while a qualified host or practitioner offers a simple choice of tea and journal before a quiet guided restorative ritual, only hands and partial figures visible, tactile white linen and clear glass, soft natural window light, crisp white and sea-glass teal palette with deep teal shadows, generous calm space, welcoming rather than clinical, no yoga pose, no text, no logos" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1440,&quot;height&quot;:1440}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="G7R7WLn-sG"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="JSu2e_DuRN" vertical-align="center" colspan="40"><h2>The stay has a missing middle</h2><p font-size="18pt">Guests can move straight from transport and check-in to dinner, work, or sightseeing. The overlooked opportunity is the transition between reaching the property and feeling present within it.</p><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="1sX_0mkYsV" colspan="20"><h4>Arrive</h4><p font-size="16pt">Bags, logistics, notifications, and unfamiliar surroundings compete for attention.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="OYXDivjwl9" colspan="20"><h4>Reset</h4><p font-size="16pt">A hosted ritual creates a clear pause and introduces the hotel’s way of caring.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="bcBQWWbNPT" colspan="20"><h4>Return</h4><p font-size="16pt">The guest continues with an experience worth describing, repeating, or booking again.</p></grid-item></grid><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="sm"><p font-size="16pt"><b>Positioning:</b> hospitality wellness, not a medical intervention—the value begins with thoughtful time, place, and attention.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="rEdxA22nEo" padding="0" colspan="20"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/MZuFpkZ3RNrsUnMyT_F-d.png" saved-media-id="4c3p5l3argnva5s" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="restorative-hospitality-editorial" alt="Observed editorial hospitality photograph of an adult guest arriving in a boutique hotel room, partial figure by the window setting a phone and travel bag down beside a glass of water, natural afternoon light, tactile white linens, sea-glass accents and deep teal detail, quiet unstaged atmosphere, no text or logos" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="wx8unRoXf8"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="_liX07F-32" padding="0" colspan="18"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/HCGpgWucQnwHcu5Ur8mE7.png" saved-media-id="av1cpyr7i1emopa" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="restorative-hospitality-editorial" alt="Quiet editorial hospitality photograph in a boutique hotel library lounge, partial figure seated near a window with hands resting beside a journal, tea glass and folded towel, natural morning light, crisp white surfaces, sea-glass accents and deep teal shadows, observed rather than posed, no text or logos" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item><grid-item id="TdJRWbkCSe" vertical-align="center" colspan="42"><h2>The 60-minute guest ritual</h2><p font-size="18pt"><b>One disciplined spine; each property’s setting and practice add character.</b></p><grid divider="sm palette-5" marker="number" marker-style="subtle" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-inline-size: 30pt; --marker-gap: 12pt;"><grid-item id="KTzcjLNeP7" padding="5pt 0"><h4>0–5 min · Welcome</h4><p font-size="16pt">Personal greeting, orientation, and a simple choice of pace or position.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Kyqp6jMViC" padding="5pt 0"><h4>5–15 min · Arrive</h4><p font-size="16pt">Breath, mobility, or grounding—by qualified practitioners, within scope.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="uVTRTHpiZ1" padding="5pt 0"><h4>15–40 min · Restore</h4><p font-size="16pt">Guided stretching, sound, quiet movement, or seated relaxation.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="uLpxFyzmsr" padding="5pt 0"><h4>40–55 min · Linger</h4><p font-size="16pt">Tea, water, journaling, or silence tied to place and time of day.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Q5clpnJFJq" padding="5pt 0"><h4>55–60 min · Close</h4><p font-size="16pt">A clear ending, optional takeaway, and warm return to the stay.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="bm0g7mX2-a" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="x9B_gsFsnz"><h2>Value is connected—not automatic</h2><p font-size="17pt">The ritual serves guests, staff, and the property only if the pilot proves the chain from interest to contribution.</p><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="T9mfhzC_fd" colspan="32"><p role="eyebrow">Who should benefit</p><grid direction="vertical" spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="aTHZhMVBMp" cell-style="subtle" padding="10pt 14pt"><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="OWloOFzF7P" vertical-align="center" colspan="17"><h4>Guests</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="bacaIwFirj" vertical-align="center" colspan="43"><p font-size="16pt">A low-friction pause without arranging an off-property appointment or clinical treatment.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="k8Fso9l5aF" cell-style="subtle" padding="10pt 14pt"><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="QxtAxq_3Fd" vertical-align="center" colspan="17"><h4>Staff</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="KKI_A5f8vx" vertical-align="center" colspan="43"><p font-size="16pt">A defined offer, booking script, capacity limit, and practitioner handoff.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="uR1xLfz0S4" cell-style="subtle" padding="10pt 14pt"><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="cJ9Mf5gDdD" vertical-align="center" colspan="17"><h4>The property</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="2l0cJQrPBl" vertical-align="center" colspan="43"><p font-size="16pt">A distinctive guest story with a testable ancillary charge or package allocation.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="3v_EMMNfqQ" colspan="28"><p role="eyebrow">What the pilot must prove</p><grid divider="sm palette-5" marker="number" marker-size="small" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-inline-size: 26pt; --marker-gap: 8pt;"><grid-item id="0NejcFllLB" padding="8pt 10pt" colspan="30"><p font-size="16pt"><b>Guest interest.</b> The offer is understood and wanted.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="itV5ckFDXf" padding="8pt 10pt" colspan="30"><p font-size="16pt"><b>Bookings.</b> Interest converts into attended places.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ZcqOobvfDD" padding="8pt 10pt" colspan="30"><p font-size="16pt"><b>Manageable operation.</b> Handoffs, capacity, and room turns stay controlled.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="uFkdCwUMop" padding="8pt 10pt" colspan="30"><p font-size="16pt"><b>Positive contribution.</b> Revenue exceeds the direct costs included in the agreed model.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><p font-size="16pt"><b>Decision principle:</b> measure the chain; do not assume the outcome.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="ORLDe9xU1a" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="HNahflIz6R"><h2>Hospitality onstage; choreography backstage</h2><p font-size="16pt"><b>Illustrative operating model</b> · 2 sessions/day · 8 places/session · 15-minute room turn</p><p font-size="16pt">Guests see a calm hour; backstage, one sequence governs inventory, room standards, qualified delivery, handoffs, and records.</p><table col-widths="[12,30,58]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" style="--table-cell-padding: 3pt 12pt;"><tbody><tr><td><p>Stage</p></td><td><p>Guest-facing lane</p></td><td><p>Backstage choreography and owner</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Offer</b></p></td><td><p>A clear, bookable ritual.</p></td><td><p><b>Reservations/front desk:</b> use one script and one shared inventory before arrival, at check-in, or in stay.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Prepare</b></p></td><td><p>A room that feels ready.</p></td><td><p><b>Hotel host:</b> checks accessible route, water, linens, seating, temperature, and approved materials.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Deliver</b></p></td><td><p>A warm welcome and guided hour.</p></td><td><p><b>Practitioner:</b> owns practice and safety boundaries. <b>Host:</b> owns welcome and handoff.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Reset</b></p></td><td><p>A consistent room at every session.</p></td><td><p><b>Hotel host:</b> restores the documented room standard before inventory reopens.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Learn</b></p></td><td><p>A brief, respectful follow-up.</p></td><td><p><b>Pilot owner:</b> logs attendance, anonymous feedback, staff handling time, direct costs—no unnecessary health data.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="oMip1Sy-4R"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="H1m-7CruSC"><h2>Replace the scenario with your property data</h2><labels><label variant="solid">Illustrative example—not actual company or hotel performance</label></labels><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="CDSQ7aOjI4" vertical-align="center" colspan="34"><table col-widths="[30,70]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" style="--table-cell-padding: 2pt 10pt;"><tbody><tr><td><p>Line</p></td><td><p>Illustrative formula</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="16pt"><b>Capacity</b></p></td><td><p font-size="16pt">2 sessions × 8 places × 30 days = <b>480 places/month</b></p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="16pt"><b>Base-case revenue</b></p></td><td><p font-size="16pt">480 × 50% = 240 participants; 240 × $55 = <b>$13,200</b></p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="16pt"><b>Direct costs</b></p></td><td><p font-size="16pt">60 × $125 = $7,500; 240 × $5 = $1,200; fixed support = $1,000</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="16pt"><b>Contribution</b></p></td><td><p font-size="16pt">$13,200 − $7,500 − $1,200 − $1,000 = <b>$3,500/month</b></p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item><grid-item id="5MMDRvxW-5" vertical-align="center" colspan="26"><h3>Contribution sensitivity</h3><graph chart-type="column" show-data-labels="true" goal-value="0" goal-label="Direct-cost break-even" text-size="md" config="{&quot;legend&quot;:{&quot;position&quot;:&quot;none&quot;}}" width="330pt" height="170pt"><properties><property key="fill" label="Seat fill" type="label"></property><property key="contribution" label="Contribution (USD)" type="data"></property></properties><data><row><cell>35%</cell><cell>-100</cell></row><row><cell>50%</cell><cell>3500</cell></row><row><cell>65%</cell><cell>7100</cell></row></data></graph><p font-size="16pt"><b>Break-even:</b> approximately 170 participants (36% seat fill).</p></grid-item></grid><aside icon="false"><p font-size="15pt"><b>Scope:</b> contribution excludes internal hotel labor, room opportunity cost, taxes, payment fees and capital expenditure. Illustrative USD assumptions use a 30-day month; do not apply the monthly result directly to the four-week pilot.</p></aside></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="skplh5Epez"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="1Syg1uDiJJ"><p role="eyebrow"><span text-color="palette-2">Six-week pilot</span></p><h2>Prove the experience before scaling it</h2><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="x8ZcCTRTGE" colspan="20"><h4>Weeks 1–2 · Prepare</h4><p font-size="16pt">Verify practitioner credentials and local requirements; choose the ritual and room; test booking handoff.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="xZC50Lr3zE" colspan="20"><h4>Weeks 3–6 · Operate</h4><p font-size="16pt">Run the agreed calendar, review attendance and issues weekly, and collect one short guest rating.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="-z7ac5YEsY" colspan="20"><h4>End of week 6 · Decide</h4><p font-size="16pt">Continue, adapt, or stop using evidence from guests, staff, safety, and the commercial model.</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="qQUiQ9Ycq_" colspan="44"><h3>Agree illustrative decision gates before launch</h3><table col-widths="[25,25,30,20]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" style="--table-cell-padding: 5pt 8pt;"><tbody><tr><td><p>Measure</p></td><td><p>Gate</p></td><td><p>Measure</p></td><td><p>Gate</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Seat fill</p></td><td><p><b>At least 40%</b></p></td><td><p>No-show rate</p></td><td><p><b>15% or below</b></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Guest rating</p></td><td><p><b>At least 4.5/5</b></p></td><td><p>Safety/service issues</p></td><td><p><b>None unresolved</b></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Incremental administration</p></td><td><p><b>Within agreed limit</b></p></td><td><p>Contribution after direct costs</p></td><td><p><b>Positive</b></p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item><grid-item id="29qhi1I0cW" colspan="16"><aside variant="caution" icon="false"><p font-size="15pt">The 40% fill gate exceeds the illustrative 36% direct-cost break-even, but it is not a total-profitability test. Excluded: hotel labor, room opportunity cost, fees, taxes, and capital expenditure.</p></aside></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="8Vt5OHhODc"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="NliTx7CvUf" vertical-align="start" colspan="40"><p role="eyebrow"><span text-color="#2F6F69">The decision</span></p><h1 font-size="38pt">One hour. Six weeks. Decide.</h1><h3 role="subheading">Make room for a restorative hour that belongs to this property—then keep it only if the evidence supports it.</h3><grid divider="sm palette-5" marker="number" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 8pt;"><grid-item id="8Jq7P7DTzx" colspan="20"><h4>Name an owner</h4><p font-size="16pt">One property sponsor owns guest experience, operations, and the pilot decision.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="4pEB1HBQgm" colspan="20"><h4>Name the room and rhythm</h4><p font-size="16pt">Choose the flexible space and session times that fit the stay.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="kRdpaviO6F" colspan="20"><h4>Agree the evidence</h4><p font-size="16pt">Replace assumptions with property costs, pricing, capacity, and success gates.</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="iPGgKjejjm" background-color="accent" padding="10pt 14pt"><p font-size="16pt"><b>Next working session:</b> choose the ritual, assign accountable roles, cost the scenario, and make the go/no-go pilot decision.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="n-YVAnj7-p" padding="0" colspan="20"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/2qtMwQp2CKYnipQNJczUf.png" saved-media-id="logxw5su8qt0dcp" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="restorative-hospitality-editorial" alt="Quiet editorial hospitality photograph of a boutique hotel terrace prepared for one restorative hour, a staff member's hand opening the door toward two simple chairs, a journal, tea glass and folded white throw, soft late-afternoon natural light, crisp white and sea-glass palette with deep teal shadows, no people posing, no text or logos" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>